# Copy to /etc/btc-intel/collector.env, chmod 0640, owner root:btc-intel.
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in copy of this file. Nothing here is required: the
# deployment collects from public government feeds and needs no credential at
# all. That is a property worth keeping -- a collector with no secret cannot
# leak one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- where state lives
# The unit sets this to systemd's StateDirectory and you should normally leave
# it alone. It is listed because the collector refuses to start on a path it
# cannot prove is writable, and because it warns loudly if the root looks
# ephemeral: a corpus under /tmp is a corpus that ends at the next reboot, and
# the accumulated availability record cannot be re-collected.
# BTC_INTEL_STATE_ROOT=/var/lib/btc-intel

# Individual paths can be split -- a fast disk for the database, a large one for
# backups -- without choosing between them.
# BTC_INTEL_DATABASE=/var/lib/btc-intel/intelligence.duckdb
# BTC_INTEL_BACKUP_DIR=/mnt/backup/btc-intel

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- provenance
# Recorded in every manifest so a corpus can name the code that produced it.
# The installer sets this from the deployed checkout.
# BTC_INTEL_SOURCE_SHA=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- credentials
# Only set this if a paid contract genuinely exists. The variable being present
# does not enable the provider -- the profile has to name it too -- and an
# unset variable is reported as "not enabled", never guessed at or defaulted.
# BTC_INTEL_SEARCH_API_KEY=
